  "status_text": "The last graph is in. All 500 gave the same answer. At 19:51 UTC, seven were still open. At 20:30, a contributor settled the last one in Lean. The game is to light any of eight points and tell whether two lit points share an edge. A circuit can use AND and OR gates, each reading at most two wires. Would allowing one NOT gate, which flips a signal, ever cut the gate count? On every graph in this set the answer was no. Both sides were on the board for each graph. The final pair was L-meta-26706 and L-meta-26707.",
